                    {
                        "translation_id": "78762bea-831d-4a2f-98d4-70ea4e73c420",
                        "source_entry_id": "2212d2b6-a464-37e6-b736-ef8e154d60b7",
                        "source_sense_id": "7242ca20-160f-3f04-a940-b06e1ce52e95",
                        "source_sense_description": "benaming voor vissen uit de familie Gobiidae",
                        "target_lang_word": "goby",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "goby",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6406f1b6-17ed-3545-840e-a430b2b94388",
                                        "entry_id": "7cd38c29-4d02-3907-b112-a6df700d35e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various small fish from the large family Gobiidae, in which the pelvic fins are fused to form a disc-shaped sucker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "250f604d-5d73-4458-b1cb-9d40ffa26f4c",
                                                "sense_id": "6406f1b6-17ed-3545-840e-a430b2b94388",
                                                "text": "“It’s estimated that 10,000 yellowfin gobies died … as well as hundreds of striped bass and hundreds of sturgeon,” and the bloom probably is impacting all aquatic species in the area “to some degree,” Traverso said."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4844c4d5-6ab7-3560-81fd-40e15b834930",
                                        "entry_id": "7cd38c29-4d02-3907-b112-a6df700d35e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gudgeon, a fish of the subfamily Gobioninae, such as Gobio gobio."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d9bd2c5-8cee-4af2-a416-6f0fb307b98a",
                                                "sense_id": "4844c4d5-6ab7-3560-81fd-40e15b834930",
                                                "text": "For acclimatization in the Barents Sea he recommends using the fish fauna of East Kamchatka and the Bering Sea, especially the Atka mackerel, the Goby Gobio gobio lepidolaemus (half scaled goby) and a species of flatfish, in the[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7e00d03-b2c8-48c6-a4df-515adb94b3c3",
                                                "sense_id": "4844c4d5-6ab7-3560-81fd-40e15b834930",
                                                "text": "Other fish species include Barbel Barbus barbus, Goby Gobio gobio, Minnow Phoxinus phoxinus, Dace Leuciscus leuciscus, Chub Leuciscus cephalus, Ide Leuciscus idus, Nase Chondrostona nasus, Burbot Lota lota, Pike Esox lucius[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75405ca3-667e-4083-9497-f32c436bc70d",
                                                "sense_id": "4844c4d5-6ab7-3560-81fd-40e15b834930",
                                                "text": "[...] undermonth Chondrostoma nasus, bleak Alburnus alburnus, goby Gobio gobio, pine Esox lucius, perch Perca fluviatilis, ruffe Gymnocephalus cernuus, spiny loach Cobitis taenia, stone loach Nemacheilus barbatulus, sculpin Cottus gobio, and burbot Lota lota (Pavlov et al., 1981)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d26ff728-d288-45e0-a149-4300c2dbd8dd",
                        "source_entry_id": "2212d2b6-a464-37e6-b736-ef8e154d60b7",
                        "source_sense_id": "7242ca20-160f-3f04-a940-b06e1ce52e95",
                        "source_sense_description": "benaming voor vissen uit de familie Gobiidae",
                        "target_lang_word": "gobie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gobie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea094cf2-5333-3bc6-b7b3-97a23eeaab88",
                                        "entry_id": "ea19cd2f-55b2-3107-8128-4601021d87b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit poisson osseux marin littoral du fond, qui a souvent une ventouse ventrale, pouvant appartenir à diverses espèces, en général de la famille des gobiidés."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7988be41-94ce-4ca0-a55d-25e5075d4b91",
                                                "sense_id": "ea094cf2-5333-3bc6-b7b3-97a23eeaab88",
                                                "text": "À la manière d’une grosse aiguille, le corps rond et effilé de ce gobie présente un profil presque droit, terminé par une queue très allongée et pointue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a240cb9c-1823-4faf-9ea3-21c3c2dcf92a",
                                                "sense_id": "ea094cf2-5333-3bc6-b7b3-97a23eeaab88",
                                                "text": "Les poissons nageurs grands plongeurs enfin, pour rechercher les prédateurs sur les zones fréquentées par des espèces benthiques et par des espèces inféodées à la roche ou aux algues, qui, même adultes, restent de petites tailles : rouquiers, courlazos, blennies, gobies, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
